==> Git

1. git init  // initialize git, now git will track current folder.

U -> untracked Sign
A -> Index Added
M -> modify file




++++++++
    Git Commands
    1. git init
    2. git add . 
    3. git commit -m "MESSAGE"

    4. git log 
    5. git status


    6. git cat-file -t commit 
        - -t => type [commit/stage/indexAdded]
        - -s => size [size of file] 
        - -p => print [ print content on terminal]


++++++++++
    Change head position
    
    7.  git diff hashCode01 hashCode02 ...
    8.  git reset hashCode // will contain left commit
    9.  git reset --hard hashCode // will delete after given hashCode commit. [changes lost] 
    10. git log 
    11. git log --oneline
    12. glog 
    13. git branch // will print all avialbe branch
    14. git branch <newBranchName> // create new branch from current branch.
    15. git merge <branch> // branch will merge in current branch.
    16. git checkout -b <branchName> // if branch is not there will create, otherwise switch to exist one.

/// jis branch ma merge karna ha phala usma move kara then use 'git merge <jo branch merge karni ha> 


++++++

squash: merge all commit into one , squash create a branch new commit then merge into current branch. 
 move to main branch first

    17. git merge --squash <featureBranch>

++++++
rebase: when lot of feature and commit add into master, our feature is left with lot of commit,
        then we do rebase to have our branch on latest commit. means rewrite all commit into our branch. 

        git rebase master  // rebase master branch into current branch. 


++++++
--set-upstream:  when local branch is not present in repository.

    git push --set-upstream origin feat-z // in remote repo feat-z branch will create and push changes into. 
    

